# Rottenmouth Viper's rulings: each opponent makes all their choices, then the sacrifices, discards and losses of life all
# happen at the same time (CR 101.4). Bot2 Show and Tells Rest in Peace in beside Bot1's Viper and loses 4 life to its first
# counter. On turn 3 the Viper attacks with two counters and Bot2 chooses to sacrifice Rest in Peace for one and to discard
# a Lightning Bolt for the other. Both go at once, so Rest in Peace is still on the battlefield as the Bolt would be put into
# the graveyard, and its replacement exiles the Bolt (CR 614.1a) - as it does Rest in Peace itself (its rulings: destroyed,
# it is exiled). Had the sacrifice come first, the Bolt would be in the graveyard. Bot2: 20 - 4 - 6 = 10.

[Bot1 Deck]
Island
Black Lotus
Show and Tell
Rottenmouth Viper
Island x10

[Bot2 Deck]
Rest in Peace
Lightning Bolt x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Island.Play
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: Blue)
Bot1.Hand.Show and Tell.Cast
Bot1.Choose(Rottenmouth Viper)
Bot2.Choose(Rest in Peace)
Bot2.Modes(Lose 4 life)
? Bot2.Life = 16
? Bot2.Battlefield = Rest in Peace
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Rottenmouth Viper > Bot2)
Bot2.Modes(Sacrifice a nonland permanent)
Bot2.Choose(Rest in Peace)
Bot2.Modes(Discard a card)
Bot2.Choose(Lightning Bolt)
? Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Bot2.Life = 10
Bot1.Battlefield.Rottenmouth Viper.Counters.Blight = 2
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
Bot2.Battlefield.Count = 0
Exile = Black Lotus; Lightning Bolt; Rest in Peace; Show and Tell
